# Tests — the unit suite (`npm test`) and the plain integration suite
# (`npm run test:integration`).
#
# Every suite reads a file from here, never `server/.env`. Two reasons: both of
# these suites assert that the capabilities report false, so they must run with
# NO provider configured; and every integration run drops and recreates its
# database, which must never be your development one.
#
# The unit suite mocks the database and ignores the DB_* values below.
#
# NEVER put an API key in a file under `env/` — this directory is committed.
# Credentials belong in an uncommitted `env/*.local.env`.

# --- Datastore -------------------------------------------------------------
# A database of its own, created on first run by the suite's hard reset.
DB_BACKEND=postgres
DB_URI=postgresql://localhost:5432/ontoforge_test
DB_USER=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=ontoforge_dev

# No EMBEDDING_PROVIDER and no AI_PROVIDER, deliberately: this suite's
# feature-disabled assertions depend on their absence.
